{
  "dom_id": "step-q120070",
  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044310/assets/51273365c4a282dc3dedd9d7cd5ac7d805e1526aaeee1915e8bd95d8223c26d3.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{\u2032}={x}^{2}+3x$\n- ${y}^{\u2032}={x}^{2}+x$\n- ${y}^{\u2032}={x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}$",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044310/assets/a14651ffc883a8c24ad17bdd031658c3d4ae21db2cfded213f2ba911fdb9a765.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slope field is zero along the lines $x=-3$ and $x=0.$ Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\n- Second, the lines $x=-3$ and $x=0$ divide the plane into $3$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $3$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| Region | $x<-3$ | $-3<x<0$ | $x>0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $\u2197$ | $\u2198$ | $\u2197$ |\n| Sign | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}={x}^{2}+3x=x(x+3)\n$$\n\ngives the required behavior.\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}={x}^{2}+x=x(x+1)\n$$\n\ndoes *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-1$ and $x=0.$\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}={x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}={x}^{2}(x+3)\n$$\n\ndoes *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-3$ and $x=0,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| Region | $x<-3$ | $-3<x<0$ | $x>0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $\u2198$ | $\u2197$ | $\u2197$ |\n| Sign | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
